      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The analgesic effect of systemic morphine (5 mg/kg, s.c.) was dose-dependently antagonized by CCK-8 administered to the periaqueductal gray (PAG) of the rat. This effect could be reversed by proglumide, a CCK-receptor antagonist. The effect of morphine analgesia was potentiated by proglumide administered to PAG. These results are compatible with the notion that PAG is a strategic site where CCK-8 exerts an antiopioid activity."},
